三秋听记 (SanqiuTingji)
======================

This software is an independently maintained derivative based on 会译 (HuiYi),
https://github.com/LingyiChen-AI/huiyi, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Substantial modifications include independent branding, packaging/update isolation,
Windows 11 UI/motion redesign, local AI CLI bridge, and notes workshop features.
This software is not affiliated with 会译 (HuiYi) or Cicada (知了).

Parts of the upstream HuiYi software were ported from Cicada (知了), https://github.com/wquguru/cicada,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Ported logic (rewritten in C#): the Ling client
conventions, meeting notes prompt and parser, heard-text cleanup and joining, meeting-end
detection, translation chain, speaker clustering and labelling rules, speaker name guessing, and the
session record format, together with their unit tests. "Cicada" and "知了" are names of that project.

Third-party components, downloaded or referenced, not bundled in source:
- sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa), Apache-2.0
- SenseVoice small model (FunAudioLLM), via sherpa-onnx model releases
- Silero VAD, MIT
- 3D-Speaker CAM++ speaker model (zh-cn, 16k common), Apache-2.0, via sherpa-onnx model releases
- NAudio, MIT
- H.NotifyIcon, MIT
- VB-Audio Virtual Cable: installed by the user from vb-audio.com, never redistributed

Bundled data:
- pinyin-data (mozillazg), MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 mozillazg: the toneless pinyin table in
  src/SanqiuTingji.Core/Resources/pinyin.txt (derived from pinyin.txt), used for the glossary's sound-alike matching.
